---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HeroSection from "../components/Sections/HeroSection.astro";
import EventList from "../components/Sections/EventList.astro";
import SermonList from "../components/Sections/SermonList.astro";
import Button from "../components/UI/Button.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Ariane Mader | ADHD & Procrastination Coaching"
  seoTitle="ADHD & Procrastination Coaching | Amsterdam, Almere & Online | English & German"
  seoDescription="Coaching and counselling for ADHD, neurodivergence, procrastination, overwhelm, stress management, habits, routines, and career clarity. Online coaching and in-person sessions in Amsterdam and Almere, the Netherlands."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.arianemader.com/"
  lang="en"
  alternateEn="https://www.arianemader.com/"
  alternateDe="https://www.arianemader.com/de/"
  xDefault="https://www.arianemader.com/"
>
  <HeroSection 
  title="ADHD & Procrastination Coaching"
  subtitle="Amsterdam, Almere, online  |  English & German"
  backgroundImage="/uploads/home-header.png"
/>


<section id="intro-message" class="py-8 bg-white">
  <div class="w-full">
    <div class="px-6 md:px-20 lg:px-40">
      <div class="mb-3">
        <h4 class="blueFont font-[Cambria]">
          You know exactly what to do. But you just can’t get yourself to do it.
        </h4>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none [&>p]:my-2">
        <p>
          You start everything last minute — even the tasks you genuinely care about — and “trying harder” only works for a few days. 
          Routines don’t stick, everything feels urgent, and you don’t even know where to start. 
          You’re stressed, overwhelmed, and it feels like you are wasting your potential.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="greenDarkFont">You’re not undisciplined or lazy. You just haven’t found the systems that truly fit your brain yet.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          I am an ADHD & Procrastination Coach offering online and in-person sessions in Amsterdam and Almere. 
          Together, we’ll figure out how your brains works and build practical ways of working that help you <b>follow through on what matters</b> without stress, guilt, or last-minute panic. 
          Whether you are neurodivergent (e.g. ADHD and autism) or simply find that mainstream productivity advice has never worked for you, we’ll figure out what does.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a
            href="/contact"
            class="font-medium underline transition-colors text-[#193472] hover:!text-[#30B28E]"
          >Book</a>
          a free intro call.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- General -->
<section id="problem" class="py-8 bg-gray-50">
  <div class="w-full px-6 md:px-20 lg:px-40">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[2fr_1fr] gap-12 items-center">
      <!-- Text -->
        <div class="max-w-3xl prose prose-lg">
          <h4 class="blueFont font-[Cambria]">Does this sound familiar?</h4>
            
          <p>
            You might recognize situations like these:
          </p>
          <ul class="green-bullets space-y-1 [&>li]:my-0">
            <li>You open your laptop to start... and a few hours later you are still sitting there, waiting to build up enough pressure to finally get going.</li>
            <li>You make a plan for the week, but by the afternoon it’s already falling apart.</li>
            <li>You avoid small admin tasks until they become mini-crises.</li>
            <li>You start new routines with enthusiasm, but they disappear the moment life gets busy.</li>
            <li>You keep buying new apps and planners in an attempt to regain control.</li>
            <li>You feel guilty for not doing “simple” things like laundry, taxes, or replying to someone.</li>
            <li>You feel capable of more, but cannot seem to access that potential.</li>
            <!--•	#You spend more time thinking about the task than actually doing it.-->
          </ul>

          <p>
            These are very common patterns for people dealing with procrastination and executive functioning challenges. 
            And instead of listening to the resistance, most people try to push through it — because the world keeps telling us it <i>should</i> be possible that way.
          </p>
        </div>

      <!-- Image -->
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center">
        <img
          src="/uploads/home-image.jpg"
          alt="Coaching illustration"
          class="w-full h-auto object-contain rounded-xl"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section id="solution" class="py-8 bg-white">
  <div class="w-full">
    <div class="px-6 md:px-20 lg:px-40">
      <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-16 items-center">

        <!-- Text -->
        <div class="max-w-none prose prose-lg flex-1">
          <p>
            <b>It does not have to stay this way.</b><br />
            Most advice assumes that the same methods work for everyone. But they don’t.<br />
            Instead, we figure out what works for <i>you</i>. So you can 
            <span class="greenDarkFont">start tasks more easily</span>,
            <span class="greenDarkFont">follow through more consistently</span>,
            <span class="greenDarkFont">build routines that actually stick</span>,
            and
            <span class="greenDarkFont">feel more in control again.</span>
          </p>
          
          <p class="mb-3">
            <b>We might work on things like:</b>
          </p>
            <ul class="green-bullets my-3 space-y-1 [&>li]:my-0">
            <li>starting and finishing a thesis, portfolio, or work project without getting stuck in avoidance</li>
            <li>building routines for your private life and work that actually suit you</li>
            <li>managing overwhelm, stress, and resistance before things pile up</li>
            </ul>
          
          <p class="mb-3">
            <b>Through coaching and counselling, we:</b>
          </p>

          <ul class="green-bullets my-3 space-y-1 [&>li]:my-0">
            <li>explore what is getting in your way</li>
            <li>test small, realistic changes  and adjust based on what works and what doesn’t</li>
            <li>build a system that fits your brain, your life, and your goals</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="mt-3">
            We will work with a mix of practical tools (habits, structure) and deeper work (patterns, beliefs, values) for
            <span class="greenDarkFont font-semibold">sustainable change</span>.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you recognize yourself in this description, 
            <a
              href="/contact"
              class="font-medium underline transition-colors text-[#193472] hover:!text-[#30B28E]"
            >book</a>
            a free intro call and we can explore it together.
          </p>
        </div>

                <!-- Image -->
        <div class="hidden md:flex flex-shrink-0">
          <img
            src="/uploads/plant2.jpg"
            alt="Coaching atmosphere"
            class="w-56 md:w-64 lg:w-72 h-auto rounded-xl"
          />
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


